xps13-ubuntu-camera (0.2.0) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Merge xps13-ubuntu-camera-zoom into xps13-ubuntu-camera: one package
    makes the webcam work for PipeWire apps and, through the Virtual Camera,
    for apps that open /dev/video* directly. The package is now
    architecture-specific and Conflicts/Replaces/Provides the old one.
  * Take over the v4l2-relayd diversion from a manual install, from the old
    split package, or create it on a fresh install.

 -- arbitrary-string <arbitrarystring@gmail.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 16:00:00 -0500

xps13-ubuntu-camera (0.1.2) stonking; urgency=medium

  * WirePlumber rules: use node.disabled only. device.disabled triggers a
    WirePlumber 0.5.17 bug (the async create-device hook never advances),
    after which no libcamera cameras and no audio sinks are created.
    Replaces the 0.1.1 change, which made that hang reliable.
  * Hiding the Virtual Camera from PipeWire also fixes GNOME Camera, which
    picked it as the first non-IR camera and failed to negotiate a format.
  * postinst warns about user/system WirePlumber files using device.disabled.

 -- arbitrary-string <arbitrarystring@gmail.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0500

